{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1105810-pentex-banes-chimera-and-fomori","id":1105810,"title":"Pentex, Banes, Chimera and Fomori","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-06-20T12:45:43-07:00","id":1105810,"title":"Pentex, Banes, Chimera and Fomori","content":"Personally, I LOVE using Pentex in one way or another in my games. Avalon Toys is an employer of more than a few Unseelie fae in my home campaign, particularly Nockers, Goblins and House Balor executives. That said, using Bane-ridden toys, Nightmares and Fomori come with that territory. So I have had to consider where Banes and Chimera overlap. A number of Banes from Werewolf the Apocalypse also turn up as Night Hag Chimera and similar, so I treat Banes as Chimera by another name. Dark, poisoned dreams that rot the heart of wonder.<br /> <br /> Many types of Nervosa and many Nocnitsa and some Urban Legends could be considered Banes, they are certainly cruel enough. And ones that focus of Hunger, Hate and Terror even more so. Plague Nervosa Mannequins and especially Outsiders are very much like banes. All they need is the Possession rede and either the Enchantment or Wryrd rede to make fomori.<br /> <br /> <b>Fomori (in Changeling terms)</b><br /> Dreamers possessed by nightmare Chimera are usually only controlled for a limited time. However a particularly degenerate host, or one subject to foul magical rites might become permanent hosts of these chimera. Such persons undergo a terrible change. Permanently enchanted much like The Ritual of Parted Mists, granting Enhancements more like mutations (I typically treat them like Wyrd versions of Redes such as Armor, Skitter and Weaponry). Unlike standard Enchanted mortals, Fomori can regain glamour by eating raw flesh, gaining 1 glamour point per health level from their victims. Most of them look like demented humans to humans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":1756,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","user":"MythAdvocate","date":". 06-21-2017, 11:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T05:51:59-07:00","id":1106019,"title":"","content":"Some sample Bane Chimera and specialized Redes.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Gooshy Gooze</b><br /> <img src=\"http://static.tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pub/images/masterbelch_144.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> Gooshy Gooze is guaranteed to be a million laughs. It swishes, it sloshes, it oozes and it goozes. It also forces itself down the throats of unsuspecting children when they\u2019re left alone at night. Gooshy Gooze is another wonderful \u201cnon-toxic\u201d creation of Avalon Toys. Like most of the dangerous toys from Avalon, Gooshy Gooze doesn\u2019t kill, it corrupts. Unlike most of the dangerous toys, this is not a simple fetish; it is a creature with a mind of its own and needs no child to do its work.<br /> Gooshy Gooze devours its prey from the inside, destroying innocence and sanity as it goes. By the time Gooshy Gooze has finished its consumption, it has transmogrified the hapless child into an equivalent volume of Gooshy Gooze. Most of the Gooshy Gooze then oozes its way back to any of 200 factories nationwide; it is subsequently redistributed to any of Avalon\u2019s countless \u201cbubble gum machines\u201d where it can again be picked up for a measly 25 cents. Many children learn from their friends that these particular machines will sometime even dispense the Gooshy Gooze without a quarter; you just have to turn the knob, and as often as not, the Gooshy Gooze is yours.<br /> Attributes: Strength 3, Dexterity 2, Stamina 0 (in host body 4), Charisma 0 (in host body 3), Manipulation 0 (in host body 3), Appearance 0 (in host body 2), Perception 2, Intelligence 1, Wits 1<br /> Abilities: Athletics 3, Brawl 3, Survival 2<br /> Health Levels: OK, -2, Incapacitated (can only be hurt by fire, electricity or freezing)<br /> Special: Gooshy Goozes force themselves down their victims\u2019 throats (Strength + Athletics vs. Dexterity + Dodge; three successes required). While within a host\u2019s body it slowly transforms its host into the same substance they are made of, and while the process is occurring, are capable of anything that the child is physically capable of: knifing Grandma, burning down the house, the usual stuff. The transformation is extremely slow, depleting one Health Level a day from the host until the victim is Incapacitated, at which time the change is complete. This transformation costs one of its host\u2019s Gnosis points per day. While in this \u201cbreeding stage\u201d the effective Health Levels of the Gooze are the same as those of its host (three to four for a small child).<br /> Redes: Corruption, Possession, Wyrd.<br /> Banes: Token (Must use the material Gooshy Gooze to use Wyrd)<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Meat Puppet (Nocnitsa)</b><br /> <img src=\"https://s-media-cache-ak0.pinimg.com/236x/51/91/27/519127580e9e8646da8f8aa3e6a52fa1.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> These spirits embody innocence defiled. Meat Puppets wander the Dreaming in search of those young beings (both human and animal) who have suffered wrongful deaths. A Meat Puppet will possess anything from a drowned kitten to a young child beaten to death by her father. Puppets hunger for the feel of young flesh. They wish only to possess a body and wreak vengeance on those with \u201cnatural\u201d bodies. However, they are not strong enough to take a living body, so they prey upon the dead. They possess the recently dead cadavers of young children or animals.<br /> Although individual Meat Puppets are not very strong, they often appear in groups. Since their bodies have already died, Meat Puppets attack unrelentingly and can only be stopped by utterly destroying the host body. Thus, even a group of Meat Puppet \u201ckittens\u201d can be very dangerous.<br /> Attributes: Strength 1, Dexterity 3, Stamina 1,<br /> Glamour: 4, Willpower: 5<br /> Health Levels: OK, -2, -5, Incapacitated<br /> Redes: Animate Dead, Traverse Dreaming, Wyrd.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Mukade (Nocnitsa)</b><br /> <img src=\"https://vignette3.wikia.nocookie.net/yokai/images/2/2f/Oomukade.PNG/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/250?cb=20150320203552\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> Considered by some to be the very image of the nightmare and corruption, the Mukade are terrifying spirit monsters that prowl the darkest parts of the Dreaming, devouring all in their paths. These hideous spirit-centipedes are large as train cars and reek prodigiously of rot and corruption. Many have human-like faces swelling from the Chitin of their heads, or even along the lengths of their bodies. Their mandibles are frankly immense and drip with spiritual corrosion. In the ages long ago, slaying a Mukade was something of a rite of passage among greater heroes but now the heroes are fewer, and the Mukade breed and writhe in greater numbers than ever in the Nightmare Worlds.<br /> Attributes: Strength 10, Dexterity 7, Stamina 7, all other Attributes at 6.<br /> Glamour: 6, Willpower: 7<br /> Health Levels: OK, OK, OK, -1, -1, -1, -2, -2, -5, Incapacitated<br /> Redes: Aggravated damage, Armor (5 dice), Blighted Touch, Dream Quake, Fester, Glamour Pact, Scuttle, Weapon (Bite; Str +3), Wyrd.<br /> <br /> <br /> Redes<br /> <br /> Animate Dead<br /> Allows a chimera to take over a dead body of a creature of the Dreaming and send it against the living. Roll Glamour vs local Banality. A zombie thus animated has Physical Attributes of 3 each; 7 no-penalty Health levels and a Brawl of 3 but no other Attributes. It only works with one corpse at a time. Nasty chimera may use any Social Abilities they have through the host body to intimidate, harass, seduce or traumatize living victims. The chimera may use this Rede on corpses of mortals if it also possesses the Wyrd rede.<br /> Power cost: 10<br /> Chimera Point Cost: 5<br /> Use Cost: 1 Glamour<br /> <br /> Blighted Touch<br /> If the spirit deals damage on an attack, the target must make a reflexive Willpower roll. If she fails, her negative characteristics dominate her personality (Seelie to Unseelie) for the next few hours. If she botches, the change is permanent. The chimera may use this Rede on mortals if it also possesses the Enchantment or Wyrd redes.<br /> Power cost: 2<br /> Chimera Point Cost:<br /> Use Cost: None<br /> <br /> Corruption<br /> By making a Glamour challenge against the target's Willpower, the bane implants a single evil suggestion that their target must act on before the session is through. The chimera may use this Rede on mortals if it also possesses the Enchantment or Wyrd redes.<br /> Power cost: 1<br /> Chimera Point Cost: 3<br /> Use Cost: 1 Willpower<br /> <br /> Dream Quake<br /> The chimera can cause the Dreaming to shake with such force that all those standing are thrown to the ground. Everyone within the radius suffers bashing damage from the spiritual concussion equal to half the spirit's Glamour roll, rounded up.<br /> Chimera Point Cost: 2<br /> Use Cost: 1 Glamour<br /> <br /> Possession<br /> The chimera can possess another sentient creature of the Dreaming with this Rede. The chimera must<br /> touch the target. The Storyteller makes a Glamour roll (difficulty of the target\u2019s Willpower), resisted by the victim\u2019s player rolling Willpower (difficulty of the chimera\u2019s Glamour). The chimera may use this Rede on mortals if it also possesses the Enchantment or Wyrd redes.<br /> Chimera Point Cost: 3<br /> Use Cost: None","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":1756,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","user":"MythAdvocate","date":". 06-21-2017, 11:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T07:46:16-07:00","id":1106053,"title":"","content":"Your mukade may be a bit underpowered; the rules for materialization have it so their stats from Revised onward would be Strength 10, Dexterity 7, Stamina 7, and all other Attributes at 6 (no Abilities added or necessary to the roll because spirits are weird).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T07:58:32-07:00","id":1106057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1105810-pentex-banes-chimera-and-fomori?p=1106053#post1106053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your mukade may be a bit underpowered; the rules for materialization have it so their stats from Revised onward would be Strength 10, Dexterity 7, Stamina 7, and all other Attributes at 6 (no Abilities added or necessary to the roll because spirits are weird).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Cool, thanks. I was basing them off of Hengeyokai: Shapechangers of the East. I have adjusted the stats.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":1756,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","user":"MythAdvocate","date":". 06-21-2017, 11:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T09:20:44-07:00","id":1106090,"title":"","content":"Interesting.<br /> <br /> I have anything of the Dreaming, though---no matter <i>how</i> evil---be entirely of the Wyld. (Yes, even the Fomorians!) Garou often mistake the Wyld as an ally when, in reality, the Wyld is creativity unrestrained....and yes, that means the Wyld can generate evil on a <i>colossal</i> scale.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T09:48:30-07:00","id":1106108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1105810-pentex-banes-chimera-and-fomori?p=1106090#post1106090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting.<br /> <br /> I have anything of the Dreaming, though---no matter <i>how</i> evil---be entirely of the Wyld. (Yes, even the Fomorians!) Garou often mistake the Wyld as an ally when, in reality, the Wyld is creativity unrestrained....and yes, that means the Wyld can generate evil on a <i>colossal</i> scale.</div> </div> </div> </div>Understood. Primordial Dreams would be pretty fierce. What I hope for in this material, is Banes from the <i>perspective</i> of Changelings. So the difference between Banes, Fomorians, Wyldlings or weirder things would be academic to the Fae. Similarly, I would treat Pattern Spiders as &quot;Banal&quot; Chimera (albeit ones linked with a potent Incarnae).<br /> <br /> On a similar note is the possibility that the Fomorians have some relationship with the Wyrm of Balance. But being bound by the Tuatha de Dannon in a manner similar to the Weavers binding of the Wyrm, has led them to becoming corrupt and sick. Hence Fae and Chimera linked with them have grown twisted and evil.<br /> <br /> All of those Unseelie Fae gifts, rituals and fetishes from Werewolf: The Apocalypse point towards Wyrm corruption in the ranks of the fey. Of course this might be more of a flirtation with the Outer Dark rather than a dedication. Fairy's having deals with the demonic is nothing new in folklore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":1756,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","user":"MythAdvocate","date":". 06-21-2017, 02:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T17:31:01-07:00","id":1106338,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1105810-pentex-banes-chimera-and-fomori?p=1106090#post1106090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting.<br /> <br /> I have anything of the Dreaming, though---no matter <i>how</i> evil---be entirely of the Wyld. (Yes, even the Fomorians!) Garou often mistake the Wyld as an ally when, in reality, the Wyld is creativity unrestrained....and yes, that means the Wyld can generate evil on a <i>colossal</i> scale.</div> </div> </div> </div>Less often since Possessed: A Player's Guide and Book of the Wyld. There's a quote in the former where Albrecht has a &quot;Fuck! That's just great!&quot; reaction to finding out the gorgons (and drones) are a thing, while the latter mechanically details what is basically the site of Pet Sematary as a Wyld Threshold.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T17:34:21-07:00","id":1106341,"title":"","content":"The Wyld <i>creates</i>---<i>what</i> it creates can vary from adorable, sweet and cuddly three-eyed puppies, to Cthulhoid horrors that distort space/time merely by <i>existing</i>. The Wyld itself is not good or evil---but it can produce either polarity as it pleases.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T18:49:46-07:00","id":1106358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1105810-pentex-banes-chimera-and-fomori?p=1106341#post1106341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Wyld <i>creates</i>---<i>what</i> it creates can vary from adorable, sweet and cuddly three-eyed puppies, to Cthulhoid horrors that distort space/time merely by <i>existing</i>. The Wyld itself is not good or evil---but it can produce either polarity as it pleases.</div> </div> </div> </div>I must get a copy of that book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T19:00:55-07:00","id":1106365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MythAdvocate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1105810-pentex-banes-chimera-and-fomori?p=1106358#post1106358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I must get a copy of that book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Book of the Wyld is filled to brim with awesometasticness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T07:09:56-07:00","id":1106534,"title":"","content":"Corrupted Elementals are fun foes to throw at characters. Parties including Nunnehi or Inanimae characters will be especially horrified with such beings.<br /> <br /> <b>Hogling (Smog)</b><br /> These appear as roughly humanoid clouds of noxious fumes, ominously rolling toward their targets. As with other corrupted elemental's, these banes can be found in polluted areas in great numbers. They normally remain inactive unless disturbed, but will prey on Changelings and other beings when the opportunity presents itself.<br /> Attributes: Strength 5, Dexterity 6, Stamina 2, Perception 3, Intelligence 2, Wits 2<br /> Abilities: Alertness 5, Athletics 4, Kenning 5, Brawl 1, Dodge 6, Stealth 8, Streetwise 6, Gremayre 4<br /> Glamour 7, Willpower 3, Banality 0<br /> Health: -5, Incapacitated<br /> Redes: Befuddle, Enchantment, Fester, Flight, Hide, Poof Begone, Traverse Dreaming.<br /> <br /> <b>H\u2019ruggling (Sludge)</b><br /> <img src=\"https://encrypted-tbn0.gstatic.com/images?q=tbn:ANd9GcTy4hGH-fEDBI55mnq5Rjb4COO2xO66VgZijVmUoqzbc-TN2faO\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> These appear as roughly humanoid piles of waste. They lumber and ooze toward their victims, leaving slimy trails in their wakes. As with other corrupted elemental's, these banes can be found in polluted areas in great numbers. They normally remain inactive unless disturbed, but will prey on Changelings and other beings when the opportunity presents itself.<br /> Attributes: Strength 6, Dexterity 2, Stamina 7, Perception 2, Intelligence 2, Wits 1<br /> Abilities: Alertness 4, Brawl 4, Kenning 3, Survival (sewers) 5<br /> Glamour 5, Willpower 9, Banality 0<br /> Redes: Armor (4), Corruption, Fester, Meld (Corrupted Earth), Venom, Wyrd<br /> Health Levels: OK, OK, OK, -1, -2, -4, Inc<br /> <br /> <b>Wakshaani (Toxins)</b><br /> These appear as roughly humanoid blobs of purplish fluid covered with blotches,veins and bubbling wart. As with other corrupted elemental's, these banes can be found in polluted areas in great numbers. They normally remain inactive unless disturbed, but will prey on Changelings and other beings when the opportunity presents itself.<br /> Attributes: Strength 5, Dexterity 5, Stamina 6, Perception 2, Intelligence 2, Wits 3<br /> Abilities: Athletics (swim) 5, Alertness 3, Brawl 4, Crafts (fishing) 5,Dodge 5, Kenning 4, Stealth 5<br /> Glamour 7, Willpower 3, Banality 0<br /> Redes: Aggravated Damage (Venom), Corruption, Element Sense, Fester, Traverse Dreaming, Venom, Wyrd","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty 